  "title": "Flight Recorder",
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "story": "The recorder wrote `flight.csv` while the hull was shaking, and some rows came out damaged.\n\nThe first line is always the header `time,altitude`. Every other line is either a good row, two whole numbers like `14,3200`, or a **corrupt** one: a missing number (`12,` or `,400`) or plain text.\n\nOutput:\n- `rows R, corrupt C`: how many good and corrupt rows (the header isn't a row).\n- `peak A at T`: the highest altitude and the time it was **first** reached, or `peak none` if there are no good rows.",
  "starter": "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main(void) {\n    FILE *f = fopen(\"flight.csv\", \"r\");\n    if (f == NULL) {\n        perror(\"flight.csv\");\n        return 1;\n    }\n    char line[128];\n    // skip the header, then check each row\n    fclose(f);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
